From: V <61495413+kelo221@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 03:11:48 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Ay::loadFile: refuse speeds the player cannot render

ChipPlayer divides by the dump's CPU (tick) speed and by its chip speed
divided by 8, and renders frames of (cpuspeed * 8172 / 44100) / 2 ticks
into an 8192-sample buffer: a CPU speed of 0 or a chip speed below 8
divided by zero, a CPU speed below 11 made frames of 0 ticks, which
never advanced and spun on the audio thread, and a chip ticking slower
than the samples rendered a tick's samples at once, which at the
slowest clocks overran the buffer. Dumps with a CPU speed below 11 or a
chip speed below 8 * 44100 (real AY chips run at 1 to 2 MHz) now fail
with FILE_LOAD_FAILED.
---
 src/audiosource/ay/soloud_ay.cpp | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/audiosource/ay/soloud_ay.cpp b/src/audiosource/ay/soloud_ay.cpp
index c0b242a..c898e67 100644
--- a/src/audiosource/ay/soloud_ay.cpp
+++ b/src/audiosource/ay/soloud_ay.cpp
@@ -161,6 +161,11 @@ namespace SoLoud
 		// The ops must be in the file.
 		if (kchunks == 0 || length <= 0 || dataofs > (int)aFile->length())
 			return FILE_LOAD_FAILED;
+		// ChipPlayer's frames of (cpuspeed * 8172 / 44100) / 2 ticks must
+		// advance, and the chip (ticking at chipspeed / 8) may render at most
+		// a sample a tick, or one tick could overrun the buffer.
+		if ((unsigned int)chipspeed < 8 * 44100 || (long long)(unsigned int)cpuspeed * (8192 - 20) / 44100 / 2 == 0)
+			return FILE_LOAD_FAILED;
 		// Zeroed: an odd last byte makes an op with a high byte of 0.
 		unsigned short *ops = new unsigned short[(length + 1) / 2]();
 		aFile->seek(dataofs);
